And therefore the essential merit of this holy path of counsel is only through the holiness of Shabbos and the holiness of the Tzaddikim. For the great Tzaddikim have already merited to ascend there, to the aspect of Ayeh in holiness, through their abundant righteousness, ascending from level to level until they merited the ultimate ascent to the aspect of Ayeh, which is the aspect of Keser Elyon (the Supreme Crown), the aspect of B&rsquo;raishis, etc. And because they merited to reach there, through this they have the power to draw forth and illuminate throughout the entire world this holy path: that even one who has fallen to wherever he has fallen, chas v&rsquo;shalom &mdash; even if he has fallen, chas v&rsquo;shalom, to the aspect of filthy places &mdash; nevertheless he should seek and search there too: &ldquo;Ayeh m&rsquo;kom k&rsquo;vodo?&rdquo; etc., as above, and through this he will ascend to the ultimate ascent, to the aspect of Ayeh, which is the aspect of B&rsquo;raishis, the hidden utterance, as above. And this is itself the aspect of the power of the holiness of Shabbos, for on Shabbos all the souls and all the worlds ascend higher and higher, up to the aspect of Ayeh mentioned above, which is the aspect of ra&rsquo;ava d&rsquo;ra&rsquo;avin (the Will of Wills), as is known. Therefore, through the power of the holiness of Shabbos, when the aspect of Ayeh in holiness shines, and likewise through the power of the holiness of the true Tzaddikim who have merited the aspect of Ayeh in holiness &mdash; through their power one can revive all those who have fallen to the aspect of filthy places, that even from there they can ascend to the ultimate ascent, by not giving up on themselves even there, and seeking and searching: &ldquo;Ayeh &mdash; where, then, is the counsel to return to Hashem Yisbarach?&rdquo; etc., as above. Therefore this path of Ayeh, too, is only merited through the holiness of Shabbos, which is the aspect of the holiness of the true Tzaddikim, as above. And this is the aspect of what our Sages of blessed memory said regarding the sin of Adam HaRishon, that he was banished from Gan Eden, etc. &mdash; and Shabbos protected him. For the sin of Adam HaRishon encompasses all the sins in the world, and the essential protection and rescue is Shabbos, for through the holiness of Shabbos, the aforementioned holy paths are drawn, through which one merits teshuvah and rectifies everything, as above.

Oas 6

And this is the aspect of tchum Shabbos of two thousand amos. Two thousand amos is the aspect of two alafin (two letters aleph), which are the aspect of two sichliyos (wisdoms/intellects), the aspect of &ldquo;two thousand years the Torah preceded the world.&rdquo; That is, the aspect of the two holy paths mentioned above &mdash; &ldquo;Azamra l&rsquo;Elokai b&rsquo;odi&rdquo; and &ldquo;V&rsquo;ayeh haseh l&rsquo;olah&rdquo; &mdash; which are the aspect of two alafin, two holy, true wisdoms. They are the tchum Shabbos &mdash; the boundary of holiness &mdash; through which one remains all the days of his life within the boundary and tchum of holiness and does not go outside, chas v&rsquo;shalom. And this is the aspect of tchum Shabbos, for Shabbos is the totality of the holiness of Yisrael, as above. For the path of &ldquo;Azamra,&rdquo; etc., is the aspect of aleph, in the aspect of &ldquo;the thousand (eleph) is for you, Shlomo&rdquo; (Shir HaShirim 8:12), which is the aspect of Shabbos, the King to Whom peace (shalom) belongs, when the thousand lights shine and are returned to Yisrael through tosfos Shabbos, as is known in the kavanos. For all this light is drawn through the holy path of &ldquo;Azamra&rdquo; mentioned above &mdash; that is, through the Tzaddik who judges everyone favorably and finds good points in every member of Yisrael, even in the very worst, etc., and implants this path in Yisrael so that each person finds in himself and in his friends good points, etc., as above, in order that through this everyone will be brought into the scale of merit and will return to Hashem Yisbarach, as above. For all of this is the work of the Mishkan, as above, for this Tzaddik builds the Mishkan from which the infants receive the breath of their mouths which has no sin, and this is the aspect of the small aleph of &ldquo;Vayikra,&rdquo; as is explained in the Torah &ldquo;Azamra&rdquo; mentioned above in its place &mdash; see there. And this advocacy of merit is in the aspect of &ldquo;If there is for him an angel, an advocate, one of a thousand, to tell a person his uprightness&rdquo; (Iyov 33:23) &mdash; that is, even if one finds in him only one merit out of a thousand, and even if in that very mitzvah and merit itself most of it is waste and it contains only some one-in-a-thousand good point within that very merit itself. And as our Sages of blessed memory expounded: even if in that very angel itself there are nine hundred and ninety-nine parts for liability and one for merit &mdash; he is saved as well. This is as above: that even the mitzvah and merit found in oneself or in one&rsquo;s friend, even if it is only one out of a thousand, and even that merit itself is full of waste and ulterior motives, etc., and there is in it only one one-thousandth part of a good point &mdash; through this one also leaves the scale of liability and enters the scale of merit and returns to Him, Yisbarach. And then everything is transformed to merit and one merits the thousand lights mentioned above, which are the aspect of tosfos Shabbos, as is brought in the kavanos of &ldquo;Yismach Moshe.&rdquo;
